{"author":{"id":"f21006d1826991d76b358f177209294474e8c2701fc659ff8fe8b8f40ee77f55"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1758917215,"nonce":"tOe9JTNoYQnbKh1iRc40iEI5WP4=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOCGKeh87HGTs8","github-url":"https://github.com/git-bug/git-bug/issues/478#issuecomment-3340319548"},"message":"Crucially, git-bug has its own concept of \"an issue\" that differs from any third-party \"issue\" -- a GitHub Issue and a git-bug issue are not the same thing, even though they may have some similarities, like their content.\n\nThat said, I've been thinking about our integration with third parties a bit more, and I think a reasonable solution would be to indicate (in the UIs) that an issue is \"bridged\", and show some metadata from that bridge, like a reference number and/or a \"view on the bridge\" link.","files":null}]}